SUMMARY:PhD Brown Bag Seminar – Nicholas Chiang (University of Melbourne)
  – Do Skilled Immigration Restrictions Bind When Firms Are Global?
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3061
DESCRIPTION:Nicholas Chiang: “Do Skilled Immigration Restrictions Bind Wh
 en Firms Are Global?”\n\nZoom: https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd
 =DX1wTJkLbR8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAvS.1\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/
 BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nI study how firms adjust labour sourcing w
 hen skilled-immigration policy tightens\, using increases in Singapore’s
  Employment Pass qualifying salary and worker-level career histories. More
  exposed firms shift away from foreign-source hiring toward workers source
 d locally\, while cross-border internal transfers also fall. Importantly\,
  the response extends to highest-wage roles that are much less likely to b
 e directly constrained by the salary threshold. This broader within-firm a
 djustment is stronger among multinational firms\, suggesting that organisa
 tional structure shapes the incidence of targeted immigration restrictions
 .
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/81347271549?pwd=DX1wTJkLbR8CVfWXiaW65kUhzrKAv
 S.1
END:VEVENT
